# Prompts

## Phase 1 — Content and website structure

### Goal

Prepare a complete content and page-structure blueprint for the New Relook Barbershop website before design or development begins. The website will use English copy for customers in Toronto.

### Design direction already agreed

Follow the supplied desktop/mobile barbershop reference closely: dark brick background, black shadows, orange/gold highlights, tall condensed headings and a dramatic layered hero. The hero should have oversized white brand lettering behind a central transparent barber/person cutout, warm side lighting and a black fade at the bottom. Preserve this composition on mobile using a separate crop and text scale.

The transparent person image will be generated with AI in a later phase. Treat it as a decorative model; do not present it as Amir or a real staff member. Shop and haircut photos will also be supplied later.

### Phase 1 tasks

1. Read `new-relook-barbershop-project.md` and separate supplied business facts, customer-reported details and information still requiring confirmation.
2. Define the website audience, primary booking action and secondary contact actions.
3. Plan a single-page website with section anchors and a clear desktop/mobile reading order.
4. Draft concise English copy for each section, including headings, descriptions and button labels.
5. Document the hero's layer order and desktop/mobile composition so later implementation follows the reference.
6. Create a content inventory for services, reviews, links and future images.
7. List missing information and define safe draft behavior for every missing item.
8. Save the blueprint as `phase-1-content-plan.md` in this project folder.

### Proposed page order

| Order | Section | Content and purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Header | Brand, section navigation, Book Now action; compact mobile menu |
| 2 | Hero | Oversized New Relook lettering, central transparent model, short location line and booking action |
| 3 | Services | Haircut and grooming categories; exact menu and prices require confirmation |
| 4 | Meet Your Barber | Short introduction to Amir based on available evidence; no invented credentials |
| 5 | Transformation Gallery | Future real haircut and before/after images in orange frames |
| 6 | Customer Reviews | Faithful excerpts with reviewer names and a Google reviews link |
| 7 | Visit and Book | Address, phone, directions, Instagram and Linktree booking; hours pending |
| 8 | Footer | Brand, contact details, social links and concise navigation |

The reference's product showcase is optional until product sales are confirmed. Use Meet Your Barber in place of the reference's blog area. Preserve the reference's visual rhythm through dark panels and orange section bands.

### Information rules

- Use the supplied Toronto address, phone, Instagram and Linktree URLs.
- The supplied Google snapshot reports 5.0/5 from 333 reviews. Record this as a supplied snapshot, not a newly verified live figure.
- An individual review's $30–40 range is not an official service price.
- Do not infer individual star ratings from the overall Google rating; the pasted reviews do not provide reliable per-review ratings.
- Preserve review wording when quoting. Mark truncated excerpts clearly and do not expand missing text or reuse the earlier paraphrased Jordan quote as a verbatim testimonial.
- Use Linktree for Book Now until a direct WhatsApp booking link is verified. Do not assume the listed phone is the WhatsApp number.
- Keep unknown prices, hours, staff details and policies in the internal pending-information list.
- Do not invent awards, years of experience, guarantees, products or booking availability.

### Completion checklist

- [ ] Every proposed section has a purpose, draft copy and content requirements.
- [ ] Header navigation and all calls to action have specified destinations.
- [ ] Hero structure explicitly matches the supplied reference on desktop and mobile.
- [ ] Supplied facts and unconfirmed details are clearly distinguished.
- [ ] Review excerpts are faithful and individually attributed.
- [ ] Image requirements and outstanding business details are documented.
- [ ] `phase-1-content-plan.md` is ready to guide Phase 2.

