## Phase 2 — Visual design setup

### Goal

Define the visual system and reusable interface foundations that will carry the reference's barbershop aesthetic through the entire website. Prepare the project foundation and a local component preview; the full hero is implemented in Phase 3 and the remaining page sections in Phase 4.

### Inputs and dependencies

- Read `new-relook-barbershop-project.md` and the completed `phase-1-content-plan.md`.
- Use the desktop/mobile reference supplied in the conversation as the visual target.
- This document currently contains phase instructions. Writing a prompt does not mean that phase has been executed. If the Phase 1 output is missing when this prompt is run, complete that prerequisite using the Phase 1 prompt first.
- Hero and business images are pending. Plan transparent-image slots and use clearly labeled placeholders only in the internal preview.

### Phase 2 tasks

1. Inspect the project and applicable instructions; reuse an existing application stack where available.
2. Translate the reference into a consistent palette, type hierarchy, spacing scale, texture treatment and responsive layout rules.
3. Establish the website's application foundation if no application exists.
4. Implement named design tokens and shared styles for backgrounds, headings, buttons, links, borders and focus states.
5. Build reusable components for the header, section heading, orange divider band, buttons and framed cards.
6. Add a local component preview showing the design system with sample content and a diagrammatic hero composition.
7. Check the preview at mobile, tablet and desktop sizes, including keyboard access and text contrast.
8. Save design decisions, asset needs and Phase 3 handoff notes in `phase-2-design-system.md`.

### Starting visual tokens

These values are initial implementation targets inferred from the reference, not exact sampled colors. Adjust them together after visual comparison.

| Token | Starting value | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Background | `#0C0907` | Main page canvas |
| Panel | `#181311` | Cards and elevated areas |
| Brick base | `#27150F` | Textured wall surface |
| Primary orange | `#F58A16` | Main buttons, bands and borders |
| Warm gold | `#D9A34B` | Small labels and secondary details |
| Main text | `#F7F1E8` | Headings and body copy |
| Muted text | `#C3B6A8` | Supporting descriptions |

Use strongly condensed uppercase display type for major headings and a readable sans-serif for body text. A starting pairing is Anton for display headings and Inter for body text, subject to available font assets. Avoid applying condensed display type to paragraphs.

### Layout and component direction

- Center the content in a roughly 1200px maximum-width container with fluid side padding.
- Use a restrained spacing scale and generous section separation without losing the dense reference character.
- Apply warm edge glows and black gradients over brick texture. Keep text areas readable and the center of the hero visually clear.
- Header: compact wordmark, desktop anchor navigation and orange booking button; mobile menu trigger with accessible expanded state.
- Buttons: orange primary button with dark text; secondary treatment with a warm border; visible hover, focus and disabled states.
- Cards: dark panels, controlled orange framing and modest corner radii matching the reference. Avoid pill-shaped styling throughout.
- Orange section bands: full-width accents with bold dark headings, as seen around the reference's gallery and feedback sections.
- Mobile: one-column section flow, scaled typography and touch targets of at least 44px; no horizontal overflow.
- Motion: subtle optional transitions with reduced-motion support.

### Hero preparation for Phase 3

Document separate layers for the brick backdrop, warm lighting, oversized white brand text, transparent person, lower black fade and foreground copy/actions. Reserve image dimensions to reduce layout movement. In the preview, use a neutral silhouette or labeled bounding box to test overlap; do not generate the person or finish the hero in this phase.

### Completion checklist

- [ ] Project runs locally using documented commands.
- [ ] Colors, typography, spacing, borders and responsive rules are centralized.
- [ ] Reusable components appear together in a local preview.
- [ ] Preview follows the dark brick/orange/condensed-type reference direction.
- [ ] Mobile layout, keyboard controls and contrast have been checked.
- [ ] Missing fonts/textures have documented fallbacks.
- [ ] `phase-2-design-system.md` records implementation paths and the Phase 3 handoff.

