## Phase 3 — Reference-style hero section

### Goal

Build the website's main hero using the Phase 2 foundation. The strongest visual feature must be oversized white brand lettering behind a large central transparent barber/model, against a dark brick wall with warm orange lighting and a lower black fade. Match the supplied reference's composition on desktop and mobile.

### Inputs and dependencies

- Completed `phase-1-content-plan.md` and `phase-2-design-system.md`.
- The application, tokens and shared components created in Phase 2.
- The supplied desktop/mobile reference, when available in the session.
- A transparent hero image if available. The user intends to supply/generate images later, so build a replaceable image slot and polished fallback now. Image generation belongs to Phase 5 unless separately requested.

### Phase 3 tasks

1. Inspect the existing application and reuse the shared header, typography, colors and layout system.
2. Build the real home-page hero with separate backdrop, lighting, title, model, fade and foreground-action layers.
3. Adapt the reference's short title to the longer New Relook brand, testing a large `NEW RELOOK` line and a smaller `BARBERSHOP` descriptor.
4. Define desktop and mobile compositions independently so the model overlaps the lettering while the business name and booking action remain readable.
5. Connect the booking and phone actions to the existing business contact channels.
6. Add responsive hero-image support with reserved dimensions and a fallback for missing assets.
7. Check layout, keyboard access, reduced-motion behavior and image loading at relevant screen sizes.
8. Record the implemented composition and outstanding image work in `phase-3-hero-notes.md`.

### Composition specification

| Layer | Appearance and behavior |
| --- | --- |
| Backdrop | Dark brick texture with a shaded center and warm orange light at the sides |
| Brand title | Huge condensed white lettering across the upper hero; partially overlapped by the model |
| Model | Central upper-body transparent cutout, ideally seated with crossed arms or a similarly strong pose |
| Lower fade | Black gradient blending the lower cutout into the page background |
| Foreground | Short Toronto location line and visible Book Now action placed outside the face/title overlap |
| Header | Compact navigation integrated with the dark backdrop, above the hero content |

Use the reference's proportions as the guide rather than forcing a generic full-screen layout. Prefer positioning within a bounded hero container; allow its height to accommodate content on short mobile screens. Keep decorative tools, if used, secondary and clear of the subject's face and controls.

### Image requirements and fallback

- Final asset: transparent PNG or WebP with clean hair/shoulder edges, sufficient resolution for high-density screens and no baked-in text, brick background or lighting rectangle.
- Subject: decorative barber model with reference-inspired pose and clothing, not an asserted portrait of Amir.
- Keep placement and crop configurable through a small set of styles or image configuration values.
- If no cutout is available, retain the typography, brick wall, lighting and booking action in a deliberate temporary composition. The implementation must not show a broken image or an empty person-shaped hole to customers.
- Document that visual matching remains incomplete until the final cutout and reference comparison are available.

### Completion checklist

- [ ] Real home-page hero uses the shared Phase 2 foundation.
- [ ] Desktop and mobile preserve the title-behind-model composition when an image is available.
- [ ] Brand name, short copy and booking action remain readable.
- [ ] Booking/call links work and header navigation has valid destinations.
- [ ] Missing-image fallback is usable and the model asset is easy to replace.
- [ ] No horizontal overflow, clipped actions or inaccessible focus states.
- [ ] Build and available browser checks pass; outstanding image work is documented.
- [ ] `phase-3-hero-notes.md` provides a clear Phase 4 handoff.

